From: UN1CA <unica@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Enable dynamic-resolution edge lighting on SDK37

Retain current S26 radius resources, model dispatch, cutouts, display lifecycle,
routine callbacks and existing no-argument method ABI. Propagate the original
multi-resolution capability from notification, scheduler, preview and routine
effect creation. Apply the original HD/FHD/WQHD density factor at the current
radius calculation, without replacing the R8-optimized drawing method.
---
diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/systemui/edgelighting/effect/data/EdgeEffectInfo.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/systemui/edgelighting/effect/data/EdgeEffectInfo.smali
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/systemui/edgelighting/effect/data/EdgeEffectInfo.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/systemui/edgelighting/effect/data/EdgeEffectInfo.smali
@@ -21,6 +21,8 @@
 .field public mIsBlackBG:Z
 
 .field public mIsGrayScaled:Z
+
+.field public mIsMultiResolutionSupoorted:Z
 
 .field public mIsSmallIcon:Z
 
@@ -61,3 +63,13 @@
 
     return-void
 .end method
+
+.method public final enableMultiResolution()V
+    .locals 1
+
+    const/4 v0, 0x1
+
+    iput-boolean v0, p0, Lcom/android/systemui/edgelighting/effect/data/EdgeEffectInfo;->mIsMultiResolutionSupoorted:Z
+
+    return-void
+.end method
diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/systemui/edgelighting/scheduler/EdgeLightingScheduler.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/systemui/edgelighting/scheduler/EdgeLightingScheduler.smali
